# Merge PRs

When Jeremy says **merge PRs**, that is the whole job:

1. Merge every remaining open PR into `main`.
2. Delete each PR branch after it is on `main`.
3. Delete leftover remote and local `cursor/*` (and any other stale) branches. `main` should be the only branch unless he says otherwise.
4. Update the documents so they match what actually shipped (`README.md`, `/help` / slash text, shipping specs under `docs/`).
5. Leave `main` clean: tests pass, no leftover branches, no stale Electron trees, no draft PR heads sitting around.

Do not leave merged PR heads on the remote. GitHub will not delete them for us (`delete_branch_on_merge` is off). After every merge, `git push origin --delete <branch>` until the repo branch list is only `main`.

If a PR is already superseded on `main` (duplicate cabin work, or an Electron-era branch that would restore deleted `src/` / `desktop/`), record it merged with `git merge -s ours` so the PR closes **without** reverting `main`. Then delete that branch too.

Do not start this merge/cleanup pass unless he asked. While he says dev is still working, leave PRs and branches alone.
